{{!-- v3 Stats tab — the one this whole change exists for.

      SIXTH PART MIGRATED, and the SHORTEST SHELL of the seven: 38 lines on v2, six includes, and
      every single row on it lives in a partial that is shared with something else. That is not a
      coincidence, it is the constraint (add-pc-sheet-v3 D5), and it is why this file is small and
      `css/pc-actor-v3.css` is where the redesign actually landed. The split is stated up front
      because a reader arriving here looking for "the Stats redesign" will otherwise conclude it was
      not done.

      WHAT MAY NOT BE TOUCHED, AND WHAT IT COSTS
      ------------------------------------------
      D5: a v3 template may hold layout and `{{> …}}` includes; it may not hold a row renderer, and
      it may not emit a `data-action` its v2 counterpart lacks. Every row on this tab is a row
      renderer in a shared file:

          stats_attributes.hbs   103 lines   the 9 attribute rows
          stats_abilities.hbs    354 lines   the 3 ability columns, ~33 rows
          power_spheres.hbs      123 lines   the 3x3 sphere grid          (also the v2 Powers tab's)
          stats_advantages.hbs    89 lines   Arete/Willpower/Quintessence/Renown/Virtues + health + XP
          stats_features.hbs      88 lines   Backgrounds / Other Traits / Merits / Flaws
          stats_health.hbs       288 lines   the health track             (also included by v3 combat)

      Five commits landed in these files in one day. Forking any of them is what D5 exists to
      prevent, so this shell includes all six with the arguments v2 passes, unchanged, and the work
      is done from the stylesheet — which reaches a shared partial's output without editing it, and
      is the whole reason the scope class exists.

      NO `data-action` AND NO `data-*` IS ADDED OR LOST. This shell authors exactly one of each that
      v2 authors: `itemCreate` with `data-origin="core"`. `stats_features.hbs` brings a SECOND create
      control of its own (`data-origin="feature"`, offering Background/Merit/Flaw/Other Trait — a
      different button set), and it is left exactly where it is, inside the partial.

      WHAT THE STYLESHEET DOES THAT THIS FILE CANNOT — read `css/pc-actor-v3.css` "STATS"
      ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
      Two mechanisms carry almost all of it, and both were verified in a headless Chromium against
      the real stylesheet chain rather than reasoned about:

        1. `content: attr(data-value)` PUTS A NUMERAL BESIDE EVERY DOT ROW, with no markup change.
           The sheet had almost none: no numeric readout existed for permanent Willpower, temporary
           Willpower, Arete, or ANY of the ~33 abilities — ~310 identical 14px circles, and reading
           a rating meant counting them. Every dot row's container already carries the value:
           `.resource-value[data-value]` for attributes, abilities, spheres, virtues, backgrounds
           and the permanent advantage row, and `.resource-counter.tempSquareRow[data-value]` for
           the temporary one. THREE READOUTS ARE STILL MISSING and cannot be reached this way — see
           the list at the end of this comment.

        2. `:has()` DE-EMPHASISES A ZERO-RATED ABILITY ROW. 19 of 33 abilities are at zero on a
           typical mage and cost exactly as much vertical space as the 14 that matter. Nothing is
           hidden, collapsed or reordered — a rating you cannot see is a rating you cannot raise —
           the fourteen that are rated are set in BOLD and the nineteen that are not keep their
           regular weight and lose a little contrast. Weight first, colour second: fourteen bold
           labels among nineteen regular ones is a pre-attentive scan; nineteen slightly-grey ones
           is not.

           The Spheres are deliberately EXEMPT. Bounded 3x3 grid, a mage raises them constantly, and
           every sphere name is click-to-cast — dimming an unused one dims an action.

      THE SECTION WRAPPERS BELOW EXIST FOR THE STYLESHEET AND FOR NOTHING ELSE. `.v3-attributes`,
      `.v3-abilities`, `.v3-spheres`, `.v3-advantages` and `.v3-statfeatures` carry no content and
      no behaviour; they are the handles that let a rule reach ONE shared partial's output without
      reaching the other five. Deleting one to "flatten the markup" silently moves that block back
      onto its v2 float layout.

      WHAT I COULD NOT DO FROM HERE, STATED RATHER THAN WORKED AROUND
      ---------------------------------------------------------------
      Three numerals the sheet still does not show, all for the same reason — the value is not in
      the DOM, so no stylesheet can print it:

        * THE WILLPOWER DICE POOL. `wod-item-base.js:341` computes `system.roll` for every advantage
          that rolls (for Willpower: `min(permanent, temporary)`, or their sum when
          `usebothrolls`). It is never rendered anywhere, on either sheet. Showing it needs the v3
          advantage RENDERER that D6 defers to its own phase — `getGetStatArea_v2`'s output is
          byte-frozen by `test-statarea-identity.mjs`, deliberately, and this is not the change to
          break that freeze for.

        * QUINTESSENCE AND PARADOX. `stats_quintessence.hbs:15` is
          `<div class="quintessence quintessence-wheel" data-name="…">` — it carries `data-name` and
          an inline `--count`, and NO `data-value`. Every other rated widget on this tab carries
          one. Adding `data-value="{{actor.system.advantages.quintessence.system.temporary}}"` (and
          the same for paradox) is ONE INERT ATTRIBUTE on a shared partial: nothing reads
          `data-value` off that element, `SetupDotCounters_v2` only walks `.resource-value`, and it
          would give both sheets the numeral for free. It is not done here because it edits a file
          the v2 sheet renders, which wants its own commit and its own eyes — not because it is
          hard. The Quintessence wheel is also 150x150 and the tallest thing in its row; the
          stylesheet brings it down, which is layout and therefore in scope.

      And one label that is missing rather than misplaced: THE TEMPORARY ROW IS UNNAMED. Willpower
      draws ten permanent circles and, beneath them, ten temporary squares with no heading of their
      own — the two are distinguished by shape alone. The numeral now distinguishes them by value as
      well, and the stylesheet sets the temporary one apart, but the WORD cannot be added from CSS
      (a literal string in `content:` is untranslatable, and this system ships seven languages) nor
      from here (the row is built by `getGetStatArea_v2`). It belongs to the same deferred renderer
      as the dice pool. --}}
<section class="tab {{tab.cssClass}}" data-tab="{{tab.id}}" data-group="{{tab.group}}" data-drop-area="true">

	<div class="v3-tabhead">
		{{!-- `wod.tab.core` is the string the nav already shows for this tab, so the two agree. Every
		      other migrated tab puts its name in the content area; on v2 this one had no heading at
		      all — it opened straight onto the Attributes banner. --}}
		<h2 class="v3-tabtitle splatFont">{{localize "wod.tab.core"}}</h2>

		{{!-- The same two v2 defects as every other tab's create control: a 3x-scaled glyph floating
		      in the corner, carrying `aria-hidden="true"` ON THE INTERACTIVE ELEMENT, which removes a
		      working control from the accessibility tree entirely. `data-origin="core"` selects the
		      abilities-only create dialog and travels with the tab.

		      The glyph is on a CHILD `<i>`, never on the `<button>`: `css/wod.css:399` sets
		      `font-family` on `.wod20 button` at specificity (0,2,1), which beats `.fa-solid`'s
		      (0,1,0), so a Font Awesome class on the button itself paints a tofu box. --}}
		<button type="button" class="v3-add" data-origin="core" data-action="itemCreate">
			<i class="fa-solid fa-square-plus" aria-hidden="true"></i>
			<span>{{localize "wod.labels.add.item"}}</span>
		</button>
	</div>

	{{!-- Content column plus the macro rail. On v2 the dice strip is `<div class="pullRight">`, i.e.
	      `float: right !important`, and all five blocks below flow AROUND it — so the width of the
	      Attributes grid depends on how many dice the splat happens to show. As a grid item the rail
	      cannot float (D4: `float` computes to `none` on a grid item, which beats `!important`
	      because it is not a cascade contest) and each column gets its own formatting context, so
	      the ~40 floats inside these six partials are contained to the content column. --}}
	<div class="v3-tabbody">
		<div class="v3-tabmain v3-stats">

			<div class="v3-section v3-attributes">
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/stats_attributes.hbs"}}
			</div>

			<div class="v3-section v3-abilities">
				{{!-- All four arguments exactly as v2 passes them. `showvisibleicon=false` is what keeps
				      the per-row visibility toggle on the Settings tab, where rows are switched on,
				      rather than on the tab a player reads. --}}
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/stats_abilities.hbs" showheadline=true useroll=true showvalues=true showvisibleicon=false}}
			</div>

			{{!-- Spheres sit with the Abilities they are rolled alongside, not on the Powers tab.
			      `spheres` / `sphereCompendiumUuid` come from `addSphereContext`, which
			      `prepareStatContext` calls: an ApplicationV2 part only ever has the context ITS OWN
			      preparer built, so moving the include without moving the context renders an empty
			      block and nothing says so. --}}
			{{#if actor.system.settings.hasspheres}}
				<div class="v3-section v3-spheres">
					{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/power_spheres.hbs" spheres=spheres actor=actor config=config}}
				</div>
			{{/if}}

			{{!-- Arete / Willpower / Quintessence / Renown / Virtues, the health track and the
			      experience total, plus the Rote band. This partial is the densest float debt on the
			      tab — a 33% and a 67% inline-width column, four nested `clearareaBox` clearfixes and
			      three more inline styles — and NOT ONE CHARACTER of it is edited: it holds
			      `{{{getGetStatArea_v2}}}`, i.e. a row renderer, so D5 forbids forking it and D4
			      forbids out-specifying it. Its container is blockified in the stylesheet instead. --}}
			<div class="v3-section v3-advantages">
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/stats_advantages.hbs"}}
			</div>

			{{!-- Backgrounds | Other Traits | Merits+Flaws — the classic printed-sheet block. It
			      carries its OWN create control (`data-origin="feature"`), which offers a different
			      button set from the tab's, and that control stays inside the partial. --}}
			<div class="v3-section v3-statfeatures">
				{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/stats_features.hbs"}}
			</div>

		</div>

		<aside class="v3-macrorail">
			{{> "systems/worldofdarkness/templates/actor/parts/macro_icons.hbs"}}
		</aside>
	</div>

</section>
